  "description": "Description of Proposed Works for 44 Eastern Road\nThis application seeks planning permission for a residential rear extension at 44 Eastern Road, London E13 9HX. The application site is an existing two-storey, mid-terrace residential dwelling (Use Class C3).\n\nKey Details of the Proposal:\nRear Extension and Layout: The proposal involves a rear extension and a shift from a traditional, compartmentalised internal layout. Primary communal functions, specifically the kitchen and dining areas, will be repositioned to the rear of the property to connect with the external amenity space.\n\nFront Elevation Preservation: The main front facade, on Eastern Road, will remain entirely as existing, with no alterations proposed to the principal street-facing elevation.\n\nScale and Massing: The scale is designed to remain visually subservient to the host dwelling, considering internal daylight factors. The massing steps back at the upper storeys to minimise visual bulk and ensure it does not result in an unneighbourly sense of enclosure or overshadowing for adjacent occupants.\n\nWindows and Glazing: The design introduces large proportional glazing and strategic fenestration to maximise natural light penetration and dissolve the visual boundary between the interior and the garden.\n\nMaterial Palette: The scheme promotes a fabric-first approach using sustainable, non-toxic, and low-embodied carbon materials. The exterior will utilize matching materials to harmonise with the host building, including brick external render, responsibly sourced Douglas fir wood or similar, mineral-rich earth bricks, and brushed/polished metal detailing.\n\nDrainage Strategy: A comprehensive external drainage strategy is proposed to mitigate surface water runoff, preventing the overburdening of the existing infrastructure.",
